      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 6 at 6:40AM HST until November 6 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI OAHU AND MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING SHORES OF MAUI THROUGH\nFRIDAY AFTERNOON...\n\n..A large, long period north-northwest swell will slowly decline\nthrough tonight.\n\n* WHAT...Surf heights of 14 to 18 feet along north-facing shores,\n10 to 14 feet along west-facing shores.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu\nand Molokai and the north facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
